<title>CANADA: Canada July bankruptcies rise over year.</title>
<headline>Canada July bankruptcies rise over year.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankruptcies in Canada rose to 7,454 in July from 5,835 a year earlier, the Department of Consumer and Corporate Affairs said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The department said 1,076 businesses and 6,378 consumers went bankrupt in the month.</p>
<p>In June, 7,268 bankruptcies were recorded.</p>
<p>For the year to date, 54,281 bankruptcies have been registered (8,642 businesses and 45,639 consumers), up from 43,769 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
